\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\f1\fs24\b ## Section A: Short-Form Questions (50 Points)\b0\par
\par
\b Multiple Choice (10 x 1 Point = 10 Points)\b0\par
\par
1. Which hypervisor type is often referred to as "Bare Metal"?\par
a) Type-1\par
b) Type-2\par
c) Hosted\par
d) Virtualization Console\par
\b Answer: a)\b0\par
\par
2. What is the primary advantage of a Linked Clone over a Full Clone?\par
a) Higher performance\par
b) Better data protection\par
c) Significant storage savings\par
d) Independent persistence\par
\b Answer: c)\b0\par
\par
3. In Linux, which command is used to display the physical CPU flags like 'vmx' or 'svm'?\par
a) lsblk\par
b) lscpu\par
c) grep -E 'vmx|svm' /proc/cpuinfo\par
d) systemctl status kvm\par
\b Answer: c)\b0\par
\par
4. Which disk format is most commonly used in KVM to support thin provisioning and snapshots?\par
a) RAW\par
b) VDI\par
c) QCOW2\par
d) VMDK\par
\b Answer: c)\b0\par
\par
5. What does LVM stand for?\par
a) Linux Virtual Machine\par
b) Logical Volume Manager\par
c) Linux Video Manager\par
d) Local Volume Mirroring\par
\b Answer: b)\b0\par
\par
6. Which RAID level provides striping with parity, allowing for one disk failure?\par
a) RAID 0\par
b) RAID 1\par
c) RAID 5\par
d) RAID 10\par
\b Answer: c)\b0\par
\par
7. The loopback IP address (127.0.0.1) is used for:\par
a) Accessing the internet\par
b) Connecting to a remote server\par
c) Local testing/communication within the host\par
d) Assigning a public IP to a VM\par
\b Answer: c)\b0\par
\par
8. Which command suite has officially replaced 'ifconfig' in modern Linux distributions?\par
a) net-tools\par
b) iproute2 (ip command)\par
c) nmcli\par
d) connectivity-tools\par
\b Answer: b)\b0\par
\par
9. What is a "Network Namespace" primarily used for?\par
a) Creating multiple users on a system\par
b) Isolating network stacks between processes or containers\par
c) Speeding up internet connections\par
d) Managing DNS records\par
\b Answer: b)\b0\par
\par
10. Which sub-command of 'qemu-img' shows detailed metadata about a disk image?\par
a) create\par
b) convert\par
c) info\par
d) resize\par
\b Answer: c)\b0\par
\par
\b Fill-in-the-Blanks (10 x 1 Point = 10 Points)\b0\par
\par
11. The software layer that manages virtual machines and abstracts hardware is the \b _____\b0 .\par
\b Answer: hypervisor (or VMM)\b0\par
\par
12. A \b _____\b0  clone creates a complete and independent copy of the original virtual machine disk.\par
\b Answer: full\b0\par
\par
13. In LVM, one or more \b _____\b0  Volumes are grouped together to create a Volume Group (VG).\par
\b Answer: Physical\b0\par
\par
14. The \b _____\b0  command is used to create a new partition table on a disk using the GPT format.\par
\b Answer: gdisk (or parted)\b0\par
\par
15. RAID \b _____\b0  provides 100% redundancy by mirroring data across two identical disks.\par
\b Answer: 1\b0\par
\par
16. The configuration file \b _____\b0  is used to define which filesystems are mounted automatically at boot.\par
\b Answer: /etc/fstab\b0\par
\par
17. To temporarily assign an IP to an interface, you use the command \b ip addr _____\b0 .\par
\b Answer: add\b0\par
\par
18. A \b _____\b0  bridge acts like a software-defined switch inside the host OS.\par
\b Answer: virtual (or Linux)\b0\par
\par
19. The \b _____\b0  tool is a semi-graphical (TUI) interface for managing NetworkManager.\par
\b Answer: nmtui\b0\par
\par
20. In Libvirt, the command to start a defined VM is \b virsh _____\b0 .\par
\b Answer: start\b0\par
\par
\b True or False (10 x 1 Point = 10 Points)\b0\par
\par
21. True or False: KVM is a Type-2 hypervisor.\par
\b Answer: False (It is generally considered Type-1 as it is part of the kernel).\b0\par
\par
22. True or False: Thin provisioning allocates all disk space on the physical drive immediately.\par
\b Answer: False\b0\par
\par
23. True or False: You can add more Physical Volumes to a Volume Group to increase its size without downtime.\par
\b Answer: True\b0\par
\par
24. True or False: RAID 0 provides high performance but NO data redundancy.\par
\b Answer: True\b0\par
\par
25. True or False: The 'df' command shows the size of a disk even if it is not formatted or mounted.\par
\b Answer: False\b0\par
\par
26. True or False: Network namespaces allow two different processes to use the same port number on the same host.\par
\b Answer: True\b0\par
\par
27. True or False: VirtualBox is a Type-1 hypervisor.\par
\b Answer: False\b0\par
\par
28. True or False: A 'veth' pair is used to connect a network namespace to another namespace or a bridge.\par
\b Answer: True\b0\par
\par
29. True or False: In /etc/fstab, the 'UUID' is a unique identifier that is more reliable than using /dev/sda1.\par
\b Answer: True\b0\par
\par
30. True or False: Extending a Logical Volume automatically extends the filesystem inside it.\par
\b Answer: False (You must run resize2fs or xfs_growfs separately).\b0\par
\par
\b Matching (2 x 10 Points = 20 Points)\b0\par
\par
31. Match the tool with its primary function:\par
Items:\par
1. virsh\par
2. qemu-img\par
3. pvcreate\par
4. mkfs.ext4\par
5. blkid\par
\par
Descriptions:\par
A. Formats a partition with a filesystem.\par
B. Initializes a disk for LVM use.\par
C. Manages KVM/Libvirt virtual machines.\par
D. Displays the UUID and properties of block devices.\par
E. Creates and modifies virtual disk images.\par
\par
\b Answer:\b0\par
1-C, 2-E, 3-B, 4-A, 5-D\par
\par
32. Match the storage term with its characteristic:\par
Items:\par
1. Striping (RAID 0)\par
2. Mirroring (RAID 1)\par
3. Parity (RAID 5)\par
4. Snapshot\par
5. Consolidation\par
\par
Characteristics:\par
A. High-speed reading/writing, no redundancy.\par
B. Combining multiple VMs on one physical server.\par
C. Exact data duplication across two disks.\par
D. Capturing a point-in-time state of a VM.\par
E. Distributed error-correction data across disks.\par
\par
\b Answer:\b0\par
1-A, 2-C, 3-E, 4-D, 5-B\par
\par
